---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import RotatingHeadline from '../components/fx/RotatingHeadline';
import Reveal from '../components/fx/Reveal';
import CleanCTA from '../components/CleanCTA.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import HomeToc from '../components/HomeToc.astro';
import {
  WORKSPACE, LINKEDIN_TAB, info, ongoing, schedule, ways,
  professionalism, levels, materials, PRE_ASSESSMENT,
} from '../data/course';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const img = (name: string, w: number) => `${base}img/${name}-${w}.webp`;
---
<Base
  title="OCP 101: Professional Communication and Presence"
  description="A nine-week, one-on-one course with Marc Gray of Odyssey College Prep: three speeches, a LinkedIn rebuild, and a video portfolio."
>
    <div id="top" class="relative isolate overflow-hidden">
      <div class="wrap relative grid items-center gap-10 pb-12 pt-10 sm:pb-16 sm:pt-16 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
        <div>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-6xl xl:text-7xl">Professional Communication and Presence</h1>
        <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
          <RotatingHeadline client:load lead="Build your presence and connection" words={["in front of an audience.", "one on one.", "online."]} />
        </div>
        <p class="lede mt-6">That is the goal of this course. Over nine weeks, we will do it in three ways.</p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
          <a href={WORKSPACE} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-full bg-primary px-7 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition hover:bg-primary/90">Open your workspace</a>
          <a href={`${base}sessions/`} class="text-sm font-medium text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Session notes</a>
          <a href="#schedule" class="text-sm font-medium text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">See the schedule</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-muted-foreground">OCP 101, Fall 2026. Mondays and Wednesdays at noon, one on one, with Marc Gray.</p>
        </div>
        <Photo name="hero-present" alt="A young man presenting charts to a small team" ratio="aspect-[5/4]" eager sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 100vw" />
      </div>
      <div class="wrap relative pb-6">
        <ol class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
          {ways.map((w, i) => (
            <li>
              <Reveal client:visible delay={i * 0.08} className="h-full">
                <a href={`${base}${w.slug}/`} class="group flex h-full flex-col rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-3 pb-5 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-primary/40 hover:shadow-lg hover:shadow-primary/5">
                  <img src={img(`way-${w.slug}`, 720)} srcset={`${img(`way-${w.slug}`, 720)} 720w, ${img(`way-${w.slug}`, 1200)} 1200w`} sizes="(min-width: 640px) 33vw, 100vw" width="720" height="540" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt={w.alt} class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-[14px] object-cover" />
                  <span class="mt-4 px-2 font-serif text-3xl leading-none text-primary">0{i + 1}</span>
                  <span class="mt-3 px-2 font-semibold">{w.title}</span>
                  <span class="mt-1 px-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{w.short}</span>
                  <span class="mt-3 px-2 text-sm font-medium text-primary">Open this page <span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span></span>
                </a>
              </Reveal>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <HomeToc />

    <section id="course" class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="grid gap-12 rounded-[28px] bg-foreground px-6 py-12 text-background sm:px-12 sm:py-16 lg:grid-cols-12">
          <div class="lg:col-span-7">
            <p class="font-serif text-3xl leading-[1.12] tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl">
              The structure is not glamorous. It works like a math formula: once you know it, you can apply it to a class presentation, an interview answer, or a pitch to a room of investors.
            </p>
            <div data-reveal class="mt-6 grid gap-4 leading-relaxed text-background/70">
              <p>Polish and flair come with years of practice. A clear structure and an audience-centered mindset come first. Each speech is recorded, reviewed against a rubric, and in some cases recorded again.</p>
              <p>Alongside the speeches, you research one topic tied to business, finance, or data science until you know more about it than most people in the room. That research becomes your speeches, your LinkedIn, and your portfolio, so when a recruiter asks what you do, you have something specific to say.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <dl class="grid content-start gap-6 lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9">
            {info.map((i) => (
              <div class="border-t border-background/15 pt-4">
                <dt class="text-sm text-background/55">{i.label}</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 leading-snug">{i.value}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="instructor" class="section">
      <div class="wrap grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="lg:col-span-5">
          <h2 data-reveal class="h-section">Your instructor</h2>
          <p class="lede">Marc Gray, Odyssey College Prep. Reach me either way below, and pick the one that fits the message.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:col-span-7">
          <a href="sms:+15019204393" class="group flex flex-col rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-6 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-primary/40">
            <span class="font-serif text-3xl leading-none">Text</span>
            <span class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-primary">501-920-4393</span>
            <span class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">For anything brief: a quick question or something you need clarified.</span>
          </a>
          <a href="mailto:mgray@odysseycollegeprep.com" class="group flex flex-col rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-6 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-primary/40">
            <span class="font-serif text-3xl leading-none">Email</span>
            <span class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold text-primary sm:text-lg">mgray@<wbr />odysseycollegeprep.com</span>
            <span class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">For anything a paragraph or longer, and for your session emails.</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="weekly" class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 data-reveal class="h-section">Every week</h2>
        <p class="lede">Two habits that run the whole course, on top of the assignments listed on each page.</p>
        <div data-reveal class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          {ongoing.map((o) => (
            <div class="rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-6">
              <h3 class="h-item">{o.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary">{o.when}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{o.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="schedule" class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 data-reveal class="h-section">Schedule</h2>
        <p class="lede">Eighteen sessions over nine weeks. The plan may shift; changes are announced by email at least one session ahead.</p>
        <div data-reveal class="mt-10 grid gap-3">
          {schedule.map((w) => (
            <div class="grid gap-3 rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-4 sm:grid-cols-[6rem_1fr_1fr] sm:p-5">
              <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 sm:block">
                <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Week</span>
                <span class="font-serif text-4xl leading-none sm:block">{w.week}</span>
              </div>
              {w.sessions.map((s) => (
                <div class:list={['rounded-xl p-4', s.off ? 'bg-secondary/60 text-muted-foreground' : 'bg-secondary/40']}>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium"><span class="text-primary">{s.day}</span> {s.date}</p>
                  <p class="mt-1.5 leading-snug">{s.topic}</p>
                  {s.due !== 'None' && <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Due: {s.due}</p>}
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="scoring" class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 data-reveal class="h-section">How your work is scored</h2>
        <p class="lede">There are no letter grades. Speeches and your LinkedIn profile are scored from 4 to 0, and you see every rubric before you start the work it measures. The speech rubric lives on the In front of an audience page and the LinkedIn rubric on the Online page.</p>
        <div data-reveal class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-5">
          {levels.map((l) => (
            <div class="rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-4">
              <p class="font-serif text-4xl leading-none">{l.score}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 font-semibold">{l.name}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-snug text-muted-foreground">{l.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div data-reveal class="mt-12 grid gap-8 rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-6 sm:p-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr]">
          <div>
            <h3 data-reveal class="h-sub">Benchmarks</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">Two surveys in the first week and again in the last week, so we can compare your scores. Your benchmark video and current LinkedIn profile are scored on the rubrics too.</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="grid content-start gap-2">
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-secondary/50 px-4 py-3"><a class="inline" href={`${base}prca-24/`}>McCroskey’s PRCA-24</a>, a standard research measure of communication apprehension. Take it here; it scores itself.</li>
            <li class="rounded-xl bg-secondary/50 px-4 py-3"><a class="inline" href={PRE_ASSESSMENT} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Marc’s public speaking pre-assessment</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal class="mt-12 grid gap-8 rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-6 sm:p-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr]">
          <div>
            <h3 data-reveal class="h-sub">Professionalism, every session</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">Five points, scored at every meeting, with feedback on the spot.</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="grid gap-2">
            {professionalism.map((p) => (
              <li class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-xl bg-secondary/50 px-4 py-3">
                <span>{p}</span><span class="shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-semibold text-primary">1 pt</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="materials" class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 data-reveal class="h-section">What you need</h2>
        <div data-reveal class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          {materials.filter((m) => m.way === undefined).map((m) => (
            <div class="rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-6">
              <h3 class="h-item">{m.href ? <a class="hover:text-primary" href={m.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{m.title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a> : m.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{m.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="policies" class="section">
      <div class="wrap grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="lg:col-span-4 lg:sticky lg:top-24 lg:self-start">
          <h2 data-reveal class="h-section">How we work together</h2>
          <p class="lede">The ground rules, from scheduling to swearing. Open any one to read it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-3 lg:col-span-8">
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">Attendance and rescheduling</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>Sessions moved or canceled with less than 24 hours’ notice, and missed sessions, are billed in full. To reschedule, email Marc at least 24 hours ahead with two alternate times.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">During sessions</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>The hour we meet is reserved for this work. No television, and no other assignments or side work while we are in session. Join from your laptop rather than your phone, sitting at a desk or table, not in bed. I hold myself to the same rules, and unless there is a real emergency, I will not answer texts or calls while we work.</p>
          <p>If I sense you are distracted, I will ask you directly what is going on. That can feel confrontational, and maybe it is. I would rather have one awkward moment than lose the quality of the session.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">Taking notes</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>Have notes from every session. They are your record that you paid attention, and they go in your workspace after each session. I strongly recommend taking them by hand, then photographing them and having ChatGPT or Claude turn them into text.</p>
          <div data-reveal class="mt-6 grid overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border bg-card sm:grid-cols-[14rem_1fr]">
            <img src={img('notes', 720)} srcset={`${img('notes', 720)} 720w, ${img('notes', 1200)} 1200w`} sizes="(min-width: 640px) 224px, 100vw" width="720" height="492" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="An open notebook with a pen resting on the page" class="h-48 w-full object-cover sm:h-full" />
            <div class="p-6 text-sm">
              <p class="!text-foreground font-semibold">The research behind this. Skip if you don’t need it.</p>
              <p class="mt-2">In three experiments, students who typed notes on laptops did worse on conceptual questions than students who wrote by hand, mostly because typists copied lectures word for word instead of putting ideas in their own words. A 2024 study of 36 university students found that handwriting produced far wider brain connectivity than typing, in regions tied to memory and learning.</p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-xs">Mueller and Oppenheimer (2014), “The pen is mightier than the keyboard,” Psychological Science. Van der Weel and Van der Meer (2024), “Handwriting but not typewriting leads to widespread brain connectivity,” Frontiers in Psychology.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">Language</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>This is a one-on-one class between two adults. A few damns and shits, even the occasional F-bomb, will not offend me, as long as neither of us is aggressive and the language never becomes a distraction.</p>
          <p>This policy is unconventional, and it is intentional. I find people are more honest when they swear. I want you to talk openly about this work without filtering it through professional language you may not have yet.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">Feedback goes both ways</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>If you cross a line professionally, I will tell you. If I cross one, I expect you to tell me. I can be intense, and I have been known to push students too hard and expect too much.</p>
          <blockquote class="my-6 border-l-2 border-primary pl-5 font-serif text-2xl leading-snug text-foreground sm:text-3xl">“Marc, I would like to give you some feedback.”</blockquote>
          <p>Start with those words, and I promise I will listen and be open to correction. You can always go to your parents instead, but I will not change my behavior until you tell me directly. Uncomfortable conversations like this one are part of what this course builds.</p>
          <p>We all make mistakes. You will have a lot of grace from me. Please give me some too.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">Late work</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>Work not submitted before a session is marked late on the professionalism check. The session goes ahead anyway, and the work is still due.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">Weekly grades check</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>Every Monday you share your current grades. This is an accountability step your family has paid for, and practice for talking with professors. If a grade slips, we write the email to that professor together.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">Communication</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>All course email goes to your SMU address. Every email you send in this course follows the five-part email structure on the One on one page: greeting, rapport, context, clear deliverable, and sign-off.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="fold group rounded-[18px] border bg-card">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">Your input</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="chev grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full border text-muted-foreground transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="prose-c border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
          <p>This is your time. If an assignment feels pointless or a goal does not fit what you want, say so. The plan can change at my discretion, and I welcome your input, especially when a suggestion makes it more likely we meet the course’s learning outcomes. The three outcomes stay.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="wrap pb-16">
      <CleanCTA title="Start with the LinkedIn worksheet" description="Fill it out before we touch your profile, due Monday, October 12. We will go from there." href={LINKEDIN_TAB} action="Open the worksheet" />
    </div>
</Base>
